        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "My personal opinion on the matter:\n\n- If the 'pkg.lock.json' is meant as a lockfile to be provided by the plugins (since 'pkg.json' is something that is provided by the plugins), then I don't think this is needed. This *might* make sense in more complex situations, like tracking the exact state of *plugin's* dependencies to make the life of plugin manager that supports transitive dependencies easier. But I don't think this is the case for the text editor plugin manager.\n- If it is meant as a lockfile for the plugin manager to store the state of all installed plugins, then this looks along the lines of `:h vim.pack-lockfile`. It *might* get documented/standardized here, but I honestly would see this as a chore with not much benefit. The main use of the standardization would be for several plugin managers to work with the same user's lockfile from the start. When in reality: 1) I don't think there will be too many Neovim plugin managers outside of `vim.pack` which 2) are okay with not needed more lockfile data while 3) generating its own is not that complicated.\n\n    As text editor config is likely not something that needs to work with different plugin managers simultaneously, I don't see spending time on discussing and documenting \"one true lockfile standard\" as worth it.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-14T18:13:37Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/packspec/issues/47#issuecomment-4972485522",
